<title>USA: U.S. Gulf rig up one at 165 in week.</title>
<headline>U.S. Gulf rig up one at 165 in week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>There were 165 rigs under contract in the U.S. Gulf as of November 15, up one from the prior week, Offshore Data Services said.</p>
<p>The utilization rate for rigs working in the Gulf, based on a total fleet of 179, was 92.2 percent.</p>
<p>The number of working rigs in European/Mediterranean rose one this week to 106 rigs under contract out of a total fleet of 106, a utilization rate of 100 percent.</p>
<p>The worldwide rig count remained unchanged at 564 out of a total fleet of 605, making the utilization rate 93.2 percent.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk 212-859-1620</p>
